## Communications
## Perovskites
Organic Tetrabutylammonium Cation Intercalation to Heal Inorganic $\mathsf{C s P b l}_{3}$ Perovskite
Inorganic $\mathsf{C s P b l}_{3}$ perovskite is well-known for resistant to organic cation substitution. Here, a specific organic cation of tetrabutylammonium $(\mathsf{T B A}^{+})$ with strong ionic binding to the $P b-1$ octahedral framework can effectively intercalate into $\mathsf{C s P b l}_{3}$ and substitute the ${\mathsf{C}}{\mathsf{s}}^{+}$ cation. A post-synthesis TBAI passivation then leads to in situ formation of $\mathsf{T B A P b l}_{3}$ layer to heal $\mathsf{C s P b l}_{3}$ perovskite with lower defect density and enhanced stability.
